<title>LEBANON: Kuwait fund lends Lebanon $20 million for highway.</title>
<headline>Kuwait fund lends Lebanon $20 million for highway.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuwaiti Development Fund has initialled an agreement with the Lebanese government to lend it six million Kuwaiti dinars ($20 million) to help finance the building of a new coastal highway in Beirut.</p>
<p>The Lebanese government's reconstruction agency, the Council for Development and Reconstruction (CDR), said in a statement that the loan agreement was initialled on Saturday in Beirut by officials of CDR and the Kuwaiti fund.</p>
<p>The loan carries three percent annual interest and makes up 45 percent of the project's total cost, CDR said in the statement on Sunday.</p>
<p>Work on the five-km (three-mile) highway -- which includes four multi-storey bridges -- linking Nahr al-Mawt river and Beirut port is expected to begin in February 1997 and be finished at the end of 1999.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.299 Kuwaiti dinar)</p>
</text>
